+/// tip
+
+You can also use `StreamingResponse` as the `response_class` in your *path operation function* and use `yield` to send each chunk of data in turn. For more details, see the [Stream Data](../advanced/stream-data.md) guide.
+
+If you want to stream **JSON Lines**, you can use `yield` directly in your *path operation function* without specifying a `response_class`. For more details, see the [Stream JSON Lines](../tutorial/stream-json-lines.md) tutorial.
+
+///
+
 /// note | Technical Details
 
 An `async` task can only be cancelled when it reaches an `await`. If there is no `await`, the generator (function with `yield`) can not be cancelled properly and may keep running even after cancellation is requested.
